# lanes.manifest — lane registry for lane-autostart.sh
#
# FORMAT (pipe-separated, one lane per line):
#   name|workdir|command|watchdog_command|max_restarts_per_hour|enabled
#
#   name                  unique lane id; also the lock/log/state filename stem
#   workdir               absolute path the lane starts in (must exist)
#   command               shell command for the lane; use ABSOLUTE paths for
#                         binaries/scripts. It is run under `env -i` with an
#                         explicit PATH, so anything not on PATH must be absolute.
#   watchdog_command      optional shell command for the lane's watchdog.
#                         Empty = no watchdog for this lane. Watchdogs MUST
#                         write epoch seconds to ../heartbeats/<name>.watchdog.ts
#                         at least every few minutes while alive.
#   max_restarts_per_hour crash-loop guard. When a lane dies more than this
#                         many times in the last 3600s, auto-restart stops and
#                         state/<name>.ESCALATE is written for the main agent.
#   enabled               yes | no. Everything ships as `no` until the owner
#                         approves registering a lane.
#
# All lanes ship DISABLED. Registering a lane (flipping to yes) is a durable
# state change that needs OWNER APPROVAL — same as the scheduler entry itself.
#
# EXAMPLE (disabled):
# render-watch|/home/hatch/workspace/lanes/render-watch|/usr/bin/env bash /home/hatch/workspace/lanes/render-watch/watch.sh|/usr/bin/env bash /home/hatch/workspace/lanes/render-watch/watchdog.sh|3|no
